[COMMENTS]
STATION,A velocity-area station downstream of the Muirhead and Camphill Reservoirs. GENERAL: River section 0.8km d/s of Dalry. Station added to peak flows dataset in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12). STATION HYDROMETRY: After a long period of closure, the station was reopened on 21/11/2014 to inform flood management. The new station infrastructure is situated on top of the original station plinth. The station is gauged up to 2.657m, with a measured flow of 57.7 cumecs. The rating has been extended by flow modelling to increase the confidence of flood estimation. The new station has a different datum from the original site. FLOW REGIME: Runoff substantially reduced by PWS exports from u/s reservoirs.
CATCHMENT,
Qmed Suitability,No comment
Pooling Suitability,Gaugings up to 2.657m and flow modelling provide some confidence in the flood estimations.
[END]
